From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:23:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: make timestamp queries reliable

A pending timestamp resolve and a shared render-stage sample hold their
own references to the query pool's counter heap and availability buffer
until their lane is closed. An application may destroy the pool while a
command buffer that wrote to it is still recording and then reset, begin
or free that buffer, and closing its encoders still names both objects.
---
